Virtual Petrography — Daxberger and Kennedy, University of Toronto Scarborough (@mp-virtual: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_4ZA3K3DY6FMKNN06EFJ8X8SARS
Heidi Daxberger and Kirsten Kennedy. Virtual Petrography, University of Toronto Scarborough. [Official hand-specimen/thin-section study resource](https://planetearth.utsc.utoronto.ca/VirtualMic/).

Use selected sample-numbered views for observation, comparison, and an evidence-based identification before checking explanatory material. Preserve specimen identity, image mode, scale, orientation/rotation context, and credits. The site explains that full slide descriptions are not directly linked to every sample; do not invent access to instructor information.

The official page states CC BY 4.0 and identifies the creators/support. The landing page/sample listings were accessible; full interactive functionality was not exercised. A virtual view develops interpretation but does not alone demonstrate adjusting or measuring with a real microscope. Identity, scope, rights, and access checked on 29 October 2026. No image collection is mirrored and no external contact is required.

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology sources — books, laboratories, analytical methods, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_38Q6Z3J7ER2G1B441JXJ14NV5A).
